CONTINUE  '(median) of the posterior distribution.'                             TCOMM28 = 'Effective temperature statistics from rvspecfit. 16th percentile &'  CONTINUE  'of the posterior distribution.'                                      TCOMM29 = 'Effective temperature statistics from rvspecfit. 84th percentile &'  CONTINUE  'of the posterior distribution.'                                      TCOMM30 = 'Effective temperature statistics from rvspecfit. Standard &'         CONTINUE  'deviation of the posterior distribution.'                            TCOMM31 = 'Effective temperature statistics from rvspecfit. Skewness of the &'  CONTINUE  'posterior distribution.'                                             TCOMM32 = 'Effective temperature statistics from rvspecfit. Kurtosis of the &'  CONTINUE  'posterior distribution.'                                             TCOMM33 = 'Radial velocity calibrated to have no zeropoint offset.  Offset is &'CONTINUE  'determined by cross-matching with APOGEE data. See details in &'     CONTINUE  'Section 4.1 of Li et al. (2019). '                                   TCOMM34 = 'Calibrated radial velocity uncertainty using repeated observations.' TCOMM35 = 'Calibrated [Fe/H] uncertainty using repeated observations.'          TCOMM36 = 'Reduced chi square from the best fit template model from rvspecfit'  TCOMM37 = 'Chi square from the best fit template model from rvspecfit'          TCOMM38 = 'Median absolute deviation from the best fit template model from &'   CONTINUE  'rvspecfit, defined as Median(Data-Model)/Median(Model)'              TCOMM39 = 'Right ascension of the object'                                       TCOMM40 = 'Declination of the object'                                           TCOMM41 = 'Object name used for AAT observation. For stellar targets, name is &'CONTINUE  'usually source_id from Gaia DR2, for galaxy targets (S5-lowz), the &'CONTINUE  'name is usually object_id from DES DR1. Some observations prior S5 &'CONTINUE  'were also included and for those, names could follow different &'    CONTINUE  'conventions. '                                                       TCOMM42 = 'Name of the stream fields, corresponding to field name in Table 2 &' CONTINUE  'of Li et al. (2019)'                                                 TCOMM43 = 'Filename of the reduced AAT spectra from each field.'                TCOMM44 = 'UTMJD of the observation'                                            TCOMM45 = 'Median Signal-to-Noise ratio of the 1700d spectra. For DR1, we &'    CONTINUE  'decide to only release objects with sn_1700d > 3 to ensure the &'    CONTINUE  'high quality of this dataset. '                                      TCOMM46 = 'Moon distance'                                                       TCOMM47 = 'Moon phase in percents (0-100 fraction of surface illumination). &'  CONTINUE  '0% corresponds to new moon and 100% corresponds to full moon'        TCOMM48 = 'Moon altitude'                                                       TCOMM49 = '0 or 1 1 = Likely QSO objects based on WISE photometry.  0 = not a &'CONTINUE  'QSO See details in Section 4.4 of Li et al. (2019) '                 TCOMM50 = 'Initial target selection priorities. Integer 1 to 9 is used. 9 is &' CONTINUE  'highest and 1 is lowest. 7-9 are stream targets; 3-6 are halo star &'CONTINUE  'targets; 1-2 are galaxy targets and therefore the parameters &'      CONTINUE  'derived  here with rvspecfit should not be used. For details, &'     CONTINUE  'please refer to Section 2 of Li et al. (2019). '                     TCOMM51 = 'For some objects, multiple observations were taken. Primary = True &'CONTINUE  'if this is the observation with the highest S/N. For objects that &' CONTINUE  'only one observation was taken, Primary is always True. This &'      CONTINUE  'column is useful if you want to get only one measurement per &'      CONTINUE  'target to remove duplicates. '                                       TCOMM52 = 'Good star probability based on random forest trained on the &'       CONTINUE  'following parameters as features: chi-squared values of the fit, &'  CONTINUE  'radial velocity error, radial velocity posterior skewness and &'     CONTINUE  'kurtosis, effective temperature, median signal to noise in the &'    CONTINUE  'spectrum and median absolute deviation from the best fit template &' CONTINUE  'model. See details in Section 4.5 of Li et al. (2019).'              TCOMM53 = 'A flag to select stellar spectra with good fitting quality. &'       CONTINUE  'good_star = 0 if it meets one of the 3 following criteria:   1. &'   CONTINUE  'good_star_pb < 0.5   2. priority < = 2   3. qso_flag_wise == 1 It &' CONTINUE  'is recommend to only use the stellar parameters and radial &'        CONTINUE  'velocities for object with good_star = 1. See details in Section &'  CONTINUE  '4.5 of Li et al. (2019). For DR1, we decide to only release &'       CONTINUE  'objects with good_star = 1 to ensure the high quality of this &'     CONTINUE  'dataset. '                                                           TCOMM54 = 'E(B-V) from Schlegel et al (1998).'                                  TCOMM55 = 'Gaia source id from Gaia eDR3'                                       TCOMM56 = 'parallax Measurement from Gaia eDR3'                                 TCOMM57 = 'parallax_error Measurement from Gaia eDR3'                           TCOMM58 = 'pmra Measurement from Gaia eDR3'                                     TCOMM59 = 'pmdec Measurement from Gaia eDR3'                                    TCOMM60 = 'pmra_error Measurement from Gaia eDR3'                               TCOMM61 = 'pmdec_error Measurement from Gaia eDR3'                              TCOMM62 = 'phot_g_mean_mag Measurement from Gaia eDR3'                          TCOMM63 = 'phot_bp_mean_mag Measurement from Gaia eDR3'                         TCOMM64 = 'phot_rp_mean_mag Measurement from Gaia eDR3'                         TCOMM65 = '1 Measurement from Gaia eDR3'                                        TCOMM66 = 'DECam photometry in g (without reddening correction) from DES DR1, &'CONTINUE  'DECaLS DR9 or NSC DR2. If the object is in multiple catalogs, then &'CONTINUE  'DES is first considered, then DECaLS and finally NSC. See &'         CONTINUE  'decam_phot_src_bits for the source of the photometry'                TCOMM67 = 'DECam photometry in r (without reddening correction) from DES DR1, &'CONTINUE  'DECaLS DR9 or NSC DR2. If the object is in multiple catalogs, then &'CONTINUE  'DES is first considered, then DECaLS and finally NSC. See &'         CONTINUE  'decam_phot_src_bits for the source of the photometry'                TCOMM68 = 'DECam photometry in i (without reddening correction) from DES DR1, &'CONTINUE  'DECaLS DR9 or NSC DR2. If the object is in multiple catalogs, then &'CONTINUE  'DES is first considered, then DECaLS and finally NSC. See &'         CONTINUE  'decam_phot_src_bits for the source of the photometry'                TCOMM69 = 'DECam photometry in z (without reddening correction) from DES DR1, &'CONTINUE  'DECaLS DR9 or NSC DR2. If the object is in multiple catalogs, then &'CONTINUE  'DES is first considered, then DECaLS and finally NSC. See &'         CONTINUE  'decam_phot_src_bits for the source of the photometry'                TCOMM70 = 'The source of the decam photometry. It is a 12 bit integer ''ABC &'  CONTINUE  'DEF GHI JKL'' where ABC bits describe the source of g photometry, &' CONTINUE  'DEF bits the source of r photometry, etc. The value of 1 &'          CONTINUE  'corresponds to DES DR2, 2 to DECALS, 3 to NSC. For example, &'       CONTINUE  'decam_phot_src_bits = 585 corresponds to 001001001001, which means &'CONTINUE  'that griz photometry all comes from DES DR2; decam_phot_src_bits = &'CONTINUE  '83 corresponds to 000 001 010 011, which means that the griz &'      CONTINUE  'photometry comes from NONE, DES, DECALS, NSC.  '                     TCOMM71 = 'unWISE flux in filter w1 from Schlafly+2019 fluxes in vega &'        CONTINUE  'nano-maggies, i.e. to convert into mags one need to do  &'           CONTINUE  '22.5-2.5*log_10(f)'                                                  TCOMM72 = 'unWISE flux in filter w2 from Schlafly+2019 fluxes in vega &'        CONTINUE  'nano-maggies, i.e. to convert into mags one need to do  &'           CONTINUE  '22.5-2.5*log_10(f)'                                                  TCOMM73 = 'unWISE flux uncertainty in filter w1 from Schlafly+2019 fluxes in &' CONTINUE  'vega nano-maggies'                                                   TCOMM74 = 'unWISE flux uncertainty in filter w2 from Schlafly+2019 fluxes in &' CONTINUE  'vega nano-maggies'                                                   TCOMM75 = 'Skymapper DR2 photometry; u band'                                    TCOMM76 = 'Skymapper DR2 photometry; g band'                                    TCOMM77 = 'Skymapper DR2 photometry; r band'                                    TCOMM78 = 'Skymapper DR2 photometry; i band'                                    TCOMM79 = 'Skymapper DR2 photometry; z band'                                    TCOMM80 = 'Starhorse distances at 5th percentile from Queiroz et al+2018'       TCOMM81 = 'Starhorse distances at 16th percentile from Queiroz et al+2018'      TCOMM82 = 'Starhorse distances at 50th percentile from Queiroz et al+2018'      TCOMM83 = 'Starhorse distances at 84th percentile from Queiroz et al+2018'      TCOMM84 = 'Starhorse distances at 95th percentile from Queiroz et al+2018'      CHECKSUM= 'LRjHLOh9LOhGLOh9'   / HDU checksum updated 2021-04-24T23:14:06       DATASUM = '735453261'          / data unit checksum updated 2021-04-24T23:14:06 COMMENT --BEGIN-ASTROPY-SERIALIZED-COLUMNS--                                    COMMENT datatype:                                                               COMMENT - {name: vel1, unit: km / s, datatype: float64, description: Radial ve\ 