COMMENT mperature statistics from rvspecfit. 99th percentile of the posterior   COMMENT     distribution.}                                                      COMMENT - {name: teff50, unit: K, datatype: float64, description: Effective te\ COMMENT mperature statistics from rvspecfit. 50th percentile (median)           COMMENT     of the posterior distribution.}                                     COMMENT - {name: teff16, unit: K, datatype: float64, description: Effective te\ COMMENT mperature statistics from rvspecfit. 16th percentile of the posterior   COMMENT     distribution.}                                                      COMMENT - {name: teff84, unit: K, datatype: float64, description: Effective te\ COMMENT mperature statistics from rvspecfit. 84th percentile of the posterior   COMMENT     distribution.}                                                      COMMENT - {name: teff_std, unit: K, datatype: float64, description: Effective \ COMMENT temperature statistics from rvspecfit. Standard deviation of the        COMMENT     posterior distribution.}                                            COMMENT - {name: teff_skew, unit: K, datatype: float64, description: Effective\ COMMENT  temperature statistics from rvspecfit. Skewness of the posterior       COMMENT     distribution.}                                                      COMMENT - {name: teff_kurt, unit: K, datatype: float64, description: Effective\ COMMENT  temperature statistics from rvspecfit. Kurtosis of the posterior       COMMENT     distribution.}                                                      COMMENT - {name: vel_calib, unit: km / s, datatype: float64, description: "Rad\ COMMENT ial velocity calibrated to have no zeropoint offset. \nOffset\          COMMENT     \ is determined by cross-matching with APOGEE data. See details in\ COMMENT  Section 4.1 of Li et al. (2019).\n"}                                   COMMENT - {name: vel_calib_std, unit: km / s, datatype: float64, description: \ COMMENT Calibrated radial velocity uncertainty using repeated observations.}    COMMENT - {name: feh_calib_std, unit: dex, datatype: float64, description: 'Ca\ COMMENT librated [Fe/H] uncertainty using repeated observations.'}              COMMENT - {name: redchisq_1700d, unit: '', datatype: float64, description: Red\ COMMENT uced chi square from the best fit template model from rvspecfit}        COMMENT - {name: chisq_1700d, unit: '', datatype: float64, description: Chi sq\ COMMENT uare from the best fit template model from rvspecfit}                   COMMENT - {name: absdev_1700d, unit: '', datatype: float64, description: 'Medi\ COMMENT an absolute deviation from the best fit template model from rvspecfit,  COMMENT     defined as Median(Data-Model)/Median(Model)'}                       COMMENT - {name: ra, unit: deg, datatype: float64, description: Right ascensio\ COMMENT n of the object}                                                        COMMENT - {name: dec, unit: deg, datatype: float64, description: Declination o\ COMMENT f the object}                                                           COMMENT - {name: name, datatype: string, description: 'Object name used for AA\ COMMENT T observation.                                                          COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     For stellar targets, name is usually source_id from Gaia DR2, for \ COMMENT galaxy targets (S5-lowz), the name is usually object_id from DES        COMMENT     DR1.                                                                COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     Some observations prior S5 were also included and for those, names\ COMMENT  could follow different conventions.                                    COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     '}                                                                  COMMENT - {name: field, datatype: string, description: 'Name of the stream fie\ COMMENT lds, corresponding to field name in Table 2 of Li et al. (2019)'}       COMMENT - {name: fileinfo, datatype: string, description: Filename of the redu\ COMMENT ced AAT spectra from each field.}                                       COMMENT - {name: utmjd, unit: '', datatype: float64, description: UTMJD of the\ COMMENT  observation}                                                           COMMENT - {name: sn_1700d, unit: '', datatype: float64, description: 'Median S\ COMMENT ignal-to-Noise ratio of the 1700d spectra.                              COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     For DR1, we decide to only release objects with sn_1700d > 3 to en\ COMMENT sure the high quality of this dataset.                                  COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     '}                                                                  COMMENT - {name: moon_dist, unit: deg, datatype: float64, description: Moon di\ COMMENT stance}                                                                 COMMENT - {name: moon_phase, unit: '', datatype: float64, description: Moon ph\ COMMENT ase in percents (0-100 fraction of surface illumination). 0% correspon\ COMMENT ds                                                                      COMMENT     to new moon and 100% corresponds to full moon}                      COMMENT - {name: moon_alt, unit: deg, datatype: float64, description: Moon alt\ COMMENT itude}                                                                  COMMENT - {name: qso_flag_wise, datatype: int64, description: "0 or 1\n1 = Lik\ COMMENT ely QSO objects based on WISE photometry. \n0 = not a QSO\nSee\         COMMENT     \ details in Section 4.4 of Li et al. (2019)\n"}                    COMMENT - {name: priority, datatype: int64, description: "Initial target selec\ COMMENT tion priorities. Integer 1 to 9 is used.\n9 is highest and 1 is\        COMMENT     \ lowest. 7-9 are stream targets; 3-6 are halo star targets; 1-2 a\ COMMENT re galaxy targets and therefore the parameters derived \nhere\          COMMENT     \ with rvspecfit should not be used. For details, please refer to \ COMMENT Section 2 of Li et al. (2019).\n"}                                      COMMENT - {name: primary, unit: '', datatype: bool, description: 'For some obj\ COMMENT ects, multiple observations were taken. Primary = True if this          COMMENT     is the observation with the highest S/N.                            COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     For objects that only one observation was taken, Primary is always\ COMMENT  True.                                                                  COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     This column is useful if you want to get only one measurement per \ COMMENT target to remove duplicates.                                            COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     '}                                                                  COMMENT - {name: good_star_pb, unit: '', datatype: float64, description: 'Good\ COMMENT  star probability based on random forest trained on the following       COMMENT     parameters as features: chi-squared values of the fit, radial velo\ COMMENT city error, radial velocity posterior skewness and kurtosis, effective  COMMENT     temperature, median signal to noise in the spectrum and median abs\ COMMENT olute deviation from the best fit template model. See details           COMMENT     in Section 4.5 of Li et al. (2019).'}                               COMMENT - {name: good_star, unit: '', datatype: bool, description: "A flag to \ COMMENT select stellar spectra with good fitting quality.\ngood_star =\         COMMENT     \ 0 if it meets one of the 3 following criteria:\n  1. good_star_p\ COMMENT b < 0.5\n  2. priority < = 2\n  3. qso_flag_wise == 1\nIt is recommend\ COMMENT \                                                                       COMMENT     \ to only use the stellar parameters and radial velocities for obj\ COMMENT ect with good_star = 1.\nSee details in Section 4.5 of Li et al.\       COMMENT     \ (2019).\nFor DR1, we decide to only release objects with good_st\ COMMENT ar = 1 to ensure the high quality of this dataset.\n"}                  COMMENT - {name: ebv, unit: mag, datatype: float32, description: E(B-V) from S\ COMMENT chlegel et al (1998).}                                                  COMMENT - {name: gaia_source_id, datatype: int64, description: Gaia source id \ COMMENT from Gaia eDR3}                                                         COMMENT - {name: parallax, unit: mas, datatype: float64, description: parallax\ COMMENT  Measurement from Gaia eDR3}                                            COMMENT - {name: parallax_error, unit: mas, datatype: float32, description: pa\ COMMENT rallax_error Measurement from Gaia eDR3}                                COMMENT - {name: pmra, unit: mas / yr, datatype: float64, description: pmra Me\ COMMENT asurement from Gaia eDR3}                                               COMMENT - {name: pmdec, unit: mas / yr, datatype: float64, description: pmdec \ COMMENT Measurement from Gaia eDR3}                                             COMMENT - {name: pmra_error, unit: mas / yr, datatype: float32, description: p\ COMMENT mra_error Measurement from Gaia eDR3}                                   COMMENT - {name: pmdec_error, unit: mas / yr, datatype: float32, description: \ COMMENT pmdec_error Measurement from Gaia eDR3}                                 COMMENT - {name: phot_g_mean_mag, unit: mag, datatype: float32, description: p\ COMMENT hot_g_mean_mag Measurement from Gaia eDR3}                              COMMENT - {name: phot_bp_mean_mag, unit: mag, datatype: float32, description: \ COMMENT phot_bp_mean_mag Measurement from Gaia eDR3}                            COMMENT - {name: phot_rp_mean_mag, unit: mag, datatype: float32, description: \ COMMENT phot_rp_mean_mag Measurement from Gaia eDR3}                            COMMENT - {name: phot_bp_rp_excess_factor, unit: '', datatype: float32, descri\ COMMENT ption: 1 Measurement from Gaia eDR3}                                    COMMENT - {name: decam_g, unit: mag, datatype: float64, description: 'DECam ph\ COMMENT otometry in g (without reddening correction) from DES DR1, DECaLS       COMMENT     DR9 or NSC DR2. If the object is in multiple catalogs, then DES is\ COMMENT  first considered, then DECaLS and finally NSC. See decam_phot_src_bit\ COMMENT s                                                                       COMMENT     for the source of the photometry'}                                  COMMENT - {name: decam_r, unit: mag, datatype: float64, description: 'DECam ph\ COMMENT otometry in r (without reddening correction) from DES DR1, DECaLS       COMMENT     DR9 or NSC DR2. If the object is in multiple catalogs, then DES is\ COMMENT  first considered, then DECaLS and finally NSC. See decam_phot_src_bit\ COMMENT s                                                                       COMMENT     for the source of the photometry'}                                  COMMENT - {name: decam_i, unit: mag, datatype: float64, description: 'DECam ph\ COMMENT otometry in i (without reddening correction) from DES DR1, DECaLS       COMMENT     DR9 or NSC DR2. If the object is in multiple catalogs, then DES is\ COMMENT  first considered, then DECaLS and finally NSC. See decam_phot_src_bit\ COMMENT s                                                                       COMMENT     for the source of the photometry'}                                  COMMENT - {name: decam_z, unit: mag, datatype: float64, description: 'DECam ph\ COMMENT otometry in z (without reddening correction) from DES DR1, DECaLS       COMMENT     DR9 or NSC DR2. If the object is in multiple catalogs, then DES is\ COMMENT  first considered, then DECaLS and finally NSC. See decam_phot_src_bit\ COMMENT s                                                                       COMMENT     for the source of the photometry'}                                  COMMENT - {name: decam_phot_src_bits, datatype: int64, description: "The sourc\ COMMENT e of the decam photometry. It is a 12 bit integer 'ABC DEF GHI\         COMMENT     \ JKL' where ABC bits describe the source of g photometry, DEF bit\ COMMENT s the source of r photometry, etc. The value of 1 corresponds\          COMMENT     \ to DES DR2, 2 to DECALS, 3 to NSC. For example, decam_phot_src_b\ COMMENT its = 585 corresponds to 001001001001, which means that griz photometr\ COMMENT y\                                                                      COMMENT     \ all comes from DES DR2; decam_phot_src_bits = 83 corresponds to \ COMMENT 000 001 010 011, which means that the griz photometry comes from\       COMMENT     \ NONE, DES, DECALS, NSC. \n"}                                      COMMENT - {name: flux_w1, unit: '', datatype: float32, description: 'unWISE fl\ COMMENT ux in filter w1 from Schlafly+2019 fluxes in vega nano-maggies,         COMMENT     i.e. to convert into mags one need to do  22.5-2.5*log_10(f)'}      COMMENT - {name: flux_w2, unit: '', datatype: float32, description: 'unWISE fl\ COMMENT ux in filter w2 from Schlafly+2019 fluxes in vega nano-maggies,         COMMENT     i.e. to convert into mags one need to do  22.5-2.5*log_10(f)'}      COMMENT - {name: dflux_w1, unit: '', datatype: float32, description: unWISE fl\ COMMENT ux uncertainty in filter w1 from Schlafly+2019 fluxes in vega           COMMENT     nano-maggies}                                                       COMMENT - {name: dflux_w2, unit: '', datatype: float32, description: unWISE fl\ COMMENT ux uncertainty in filter w2 from Schlafly+2019 fluxes in vega           COMMENT     nano-maggies}                                                       COMMENT - {name: u_skm, unit: mag, datatype: float64, description: Skymapper D\ COMMENT R2 photometry; u band}                                                  COMMENT - {name: g_skm, unit: mag, datatype: float64, description: Skymapper D\ COMMENT R2 photometry; g band}                                                  COMMENT - {name: r_skm, unit: mag, datatype: float64, description: Skymapper D\ COMMENT R2 photometry; r band}                                                  COMMENT - {name: i_skm, unit: mag, datatype: float64, description: Skymapper D\ COMMENT R2 photometry; i band}                                                  COMMENT - {name: z_skm, unit: mag, datatype: float64, description: Skymapper D\ COMMENT R2 photometry; z band}                                                  COMMENT - {name: starhorse_dist05, unit: kpc, datatype: float32, description: \ COMMENT Starhorse distances at 5th percentile from Queiroz et al+2018}          COMMENT - {name: starhorse_dist16, unit: kpc, datatype: float32, description: \ COMMENT Starhorse distances at 16th percentile from Queiroz et al+2018}         COMMENT - {name: starhorse_dist50, unit: kpc, datatype: float32, description: \ COMMENT Starhorse distances at 50th percentile from Queiroz et al+2018}         COMMENT - {name: starhorse_dist84, unit: kpc, datatype: float32, description: \ COMMENT Starhorse distances at 84th percentile from Queiroz et al+2018}         COMMENT - {name: starhorse_dist95, unit: kpc, datatype: float32, description: \ COMMENT Starhorse distances at 95th percentile from Queiroz et al+2018}         COMMENT meta:                                                                   COMMENT   __serialized_columns__: {}                                            COMMENT --END-ASTROPY-SERIALIZED-COLUMNS--                                      